  "prompt": "Build LedgerLoop's logo retention table for the accounts created from July to December 2025. An account's cohort month is the month of its created_at (Brussels local time). An account is active at a month's end when the sum of its subscription events' mrr_delta_local with event_date on or before that day is above 0. The month offset counts calendar months from the cohort month, from 0 to 3. The as-of date is 1 January 2026: for a month that ends after it, active_accounts and retention_rate show missing, while a month that has ended with no active account shows 0. Return five columns, in this order: cohort_month (the first day of the month), month_offset, cohort_accounts, active_accounts and retention_rate, active_accounts divided by cohort_accounts as a fraction between 0 and 1. Return one row for each cohort month that has accounts and each month offset from 0 to 3. Any row order is fine.",
